{"case_id":"C042","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"change_types":["refactor","instrumentation_change"],"affected_functions":["handle_incoming_request","h2o_probe_log_request","h2o_probe_request_header"],"reason":"The commit centralizes existing request-probe emission in probes_.h and adds scheme logging to that instrumentation. It does not introduce a new processing entry point, protocol behavior, initialization requirement, configuration, or input constraint. The HTTP/1 harness still supplies arbitrary request bytes through h2o_http1_accept with a fully initialized context, so it remains adequate for the changed high-level path.","evidence":["handle_incoming_request replaces its inline H2O_PROBE_CONN and header-probe block with h2o_probe_log_request(&conn->req, conn->_req_index).","h2o_probe_log_request emits the same RECEIVE_REQUEST and RECEIVE_REQUEST_HEADER probes, with an additional H2O_TOKEN_SCHEME field and a reordered method/authority sequence.","The probe body remains conditional on H2O_CONN_IS_PROBED, and the disabled-probe macros remain no-ops; no new caller-supplied state is required.","fuzz/driver.cc sends arbitrary Data through create_accepted and invokes h2o_http1_accept, which continues to reach handle_incoming_request."],"recommended_action":"No fuzz-harness update is required for this commit."}
